From a2f28124b40b7d1ea0af77e1fc46687b17b64306 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edde746 <86283021+edde746@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 07:14:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] windows: heal resize synchronization wedge
 (flutter/flutter#159630)

If the window is resized between surface creation and the first frame -
which is what PowerToys FancyZones "Move newly created windows to their
last known zone" does - the resize synchronization enters kResizeStarted
and only presents frames matching the target size. If the framework never
produces one (dropped metrics, no scheduled frame, or a failed surface
recreate), every subsequent frame is rejected and the window stays blank
until a real resize re-enters OnWindowSizeChanged. ForceRedraw is a no-op
while a resize is pending, so nothing recovers it.

- Re-drive a pending resize: resend the target metrics and schedule a
  frame on resize timeout, on rejected frames, and from ForceRedraw.
- Recreate a missing or invalid surface on the next generated frame
  instead of dropping frames forever; drop the destroyed husk when a
  resize-time recreate fails.
- Force-complete the resize on the raster thread after 60 retries so the
  view can never wedge permanently.

